== P2: Collatz: P(next v = 1 | v = 1) is exactly 1/2 at every size (n = 7 mod 8 among n = 3 mod 4) ==
   [N, 2N) with N =       1000: #n=3 mod 4: 250, #n=7 mod 8: 125, ratio 0.500000
   [N, 2N) with N =     100000: #n=3 mod 4: 25000, #n=7 mod 8: 12500, ratio 0.500000
   [N, 2N) with N =   10000000: #n=3 mod 4: 2500000, #n=7 mod 8: 1250000, ratio 0.500000
   [N, 2N) with N = 1000000000: #n=3 mod 4: 250000000, #n=7 mod 8: 125000000, ratio 0.500000
   along orbits of odd n < 2*10^5, steps with current value large(>=10^4): P(next v=1 | v=1) = 0.4965 (708316 steps)
   along orbits of odd n < 2*10^5, steps with current value small(<10^4): P(next v=1 | v=1) = 0.5334 (1313412 steps)

== P3: random models: stationary memory does not change the fate; size-coupled persistence can ==
   persistence p=0.00: mean slope -0.4130 bits/step (i.i.d. value log2 3 - 2 = -0.4150); mean max height 1.3; paths ending above start: 0/200
   persistence p=0.50: mean slope -0.4199 bits/step (i.i.d. value log2 3 - 2 = -0.4150); mean max height 3.1; paths ending above start: 0/200
   persistence p=0.90: mean slope -0.4265 bits/step (i.i.d. value log2 3 - 2 = -0.4150); mean max height 17.7; paths ending above start: 0/200
   persistence p=0.99: mean slope -0.4231 bits/step (i.i.d. value log2 3 - 2 = -0.4150); mean max height 169.0; paths ending above start: 16/200
   growth state with escape c/sqrt(N), c=3: fraction never escaping in 20000 steps from N0 = 2^20: 0.974
   growth state with escape c/ln N, c=0.6: fraction never escaping in 20000 steps from N0 = 2^20: 0.000

== P4: typology numbers re-checked ==
   Juggler n <= 2000: all reach 1; mean log2(log m'/log m) per step -0.334 (fair coin -0.208); P(parity persists) 0.565; longest 80 steps; largest 271 digits
   reverse-and-add n < 10^5, 300 steps: not palindromic: 6091 (first [196, 295, 394, 493, 592, 689, 691, 788, 790, 879, 887, 978]); below 10^4: 249; mean digit growth per step (first 50 steps) +0.403
   look-and-say: length ratio at 60 steps 1.30361 (Conway 1.30358)
   Ducci length 8, entries < 4 (4^8 vectors): all reach 0, worst 14 steps
   Kaprekar 4 digits: every non-repdigit reaches 6174, worst 7 steps
   aliquot mean log2(s(n)/n) by class a (even n <= 2*10^6): a=1: -0.348, a=2: +0.129, a=3: +0.318, a=4: +0.404, a=5: +0.445, a=6: +0.465
   abundant density to 2*10^6: 0.2475 (Deleglise: 0.2476..0.2480)

